\subsection{Normalizing superseding-version relations}

Crossref's [[relation]] map can express many relationship types; we only care
about those that mean a newer, more canonical version of this work exists.  The
clearest is [[is-preprint-of]] (this preprint has a published version);
[[is-version-of]] captures the more general case of a work that is a particular
version of a canonical record.  We read only relations whose identifier is a
DOI, since a bare DOI is what makes the newer version actionable for the reader.

<<constants>>=
# Crossref relation types that mean a newer/canonical version exists.
SUPERSEDING_RELATIONS = ("is-preprint-of", "is-version-of")
@

<<currency normalization helpers>>=
def _normalize_newer_versions(message: dict) -> list[dict]:
    """Extract DOIs of newer/canonical versions from the relation map."""
    relation = message.get("relation") or {}
    versions = []
    for rel_type in SUPERSEDING_RELATIONS:
        for entry in relation.get(rel_type) or []:
            if entry.get("id-type") == "doi" and entry.get("id"):
                versions.append({"doi": entry["id"], "relation": rel_type})
    return versions
@

<<test functions>>=
class TestNormalizeNewerVersions:
    """Tests for _normalize_newer_versions."""

    def test_preprint_relation_is_extracted(self):
        message = {
            "relation": {
                "is-preprint-of": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.1/published"}]
            }
        }
        assert _normalize_newer_versions(message) == [
            {"doi": "10.1/published", "relation": "is-preprint-of"}
        ]

    def test_non_doi_relation_is_ignored(self):
        message = {
            "relation": {
                "is-preprint-of": [{"id-type": "url", "id": "http://x"}]
            }
        }
        assert _normalize_newer_versions(message) == []

    def test_no_relation_is_empty(self):
        assert _normalize_newer_versions({}) == []
@

\subsection{Normalizing preprint relations}

[[is-preprint-of]] has an inverse: [[has-preprint]] appears on the
\emph{published} work's record and points back at its preprint's DOI.
Where the superseding relations answer \enquote{should I cite something
newer?}, this one answers \enquote{is there a free earlier version of
this work?}---which is exactly what the preprint fallback during
enrichment needs (\cref{preprint-module}).  Publishers populate it
sparsely, but when present it is an authoritative, DOI-to-DOI link that
requires no title matching.  Since [[fetch_currency]] already retrieves
the full relation map for every checked paper, extracting it costs no
additional request.

<<constants>>=
# Inverse of is-preprint-of: on a published work, points at its preprint.
PREPRINT_RELATION = "has-preprint"
<<currency normalization helpers>>=
def _normalize_preprints(message: dict) -> list[dict]:
    """Extract preprint DOIs from the relation map."""
    relation = message.get("relation") or {}
    preprints = []
    for entry in relation.get(PREPRINT_RELATION) or []:
        if entry.get("id-type") == "doi" and entry.get("id"):
            preprints.append(
                {"doi": entry["id"], "relation": PREPRINT_RELATION}
            )
    return preprints
@

The same DOI-only rule applies as for the superseding relations: a
preprint we cannot address by DOI cannot be looked up or adopted, so
non-DOI identifiers are dropped.

<<test functions>>=
class TestNormalizePreprints:
    """Tests for _normalize_preprints."""

    def test_has_preprint_relation_is_extracted(self):
        message = {
            "relation": {
                "has-preprint": [
                    {"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.48550/arXiv.2401.1"}
                ]
            }
        }
        assert _normalize_preprints(message) == [
            {"doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2401.1", "relation": "has-preprint"}
        ]

    def test_non_doi_relation_is_ignored(self):
        message = {
            "relation": {
                "has-preprint": [{"id-type": "url", "id": "http://x"}]
            }
        }
        assert _normalize_preprints(message) == []

    def test_no_relation_is_empty(self):
        assert _normalize_preprints({}) == []
