\section{The module-level interface}
\label{sec:crossref-module-interface}

Callers want four convenient verbs over a single shared client: look up
one DOI, list a published work's preprint DOIs, annotate a batch of
papers, and reduce a paper to a one-word status.  We instantiate the
client once at import time so its cache and session are shared across
the whole process.

<<module-level currency interface>>=
_client = CrossrefClient()


def fetch_currency(doi: str | None) -> dict | None:
    """Look up currency metadata for a single DOI (see CrossrefClient)."""
    return _client.fetch_currency(doi)


def last_lookup_error() -> str | None:
    """Why the shared client's last lookup failed; None if it did not."""
    return _client.last_lookup_error
@

\subsection{Listing a work's preprint DOIs}

The preprint fallback (\cref{preprint-module}) needs only the DOIs from
the [[has-preprint]] relation, not the full currency dictionary, so we
give it a wrapper that flattens the result.  An undetermined lookup and
a work without the relation both yield an empty list here: for the
caller the distinction does not matter---either way there is no
preprint DOI to follow---and collapsing them keeps the fallback's tier
logic a simple iteration.

<<module-level currency interface>>=
def fetch_preprint_dois(doi: str | None) -> list[str]:
    """Return DOIs of known preprints of the published work ``doi``.

    Reads Crossref's `has-preprint` relation. Returns an empty list
    when the lookup is undetermined or no preprint is on record.
    """
    result = _client.fetch_currency(doi)
    if not result:
        return []
    dois = [
        entry["doi"]
        for entry in result.get("preprints", [])
        if entry.get("doi")
    ]
    # Crossref records occasionally repeat a relation entry verbatim.
    return list(dict.fromkeys(dois))
